   "html_text": "In some cases, receipt of potential new treatments is in the ex ante interests of research participants. For example, the risks posed by an experimental cancer treatment might be justified by the possibility that it will extend participants’ lives. Moreover, the risk/benefit profile of the treatment might be as favorable for participants as the risk/benefit profile of any available alternatives. In these cases, receipt of the experimental intervention ex ante promotes participants’ interests. In",
